			},
			"date": "2023-03-15T19:52:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Doesn't it need to bootstrap a whole new Realm with its own copy of the intrinsics?</p><pre><code>$ node<br>Welcome to Node.js v19.6.0.<br>Type \".help\" for more information.<br>&gt; let otherArray = vm.runInContext('Array', vm.createContext())<br>undefined<br>&gt; Array === otherArray<br>false<br>&gt;<br></code></pre>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110029111250271775",
			"parentId": "110029042993139645",
			"url": "https://types.pl/@mvsamuel/110029111215945301",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mike Samuel",
				"url": "https://types.pl/@mvsamuel",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/627/153/354/001/664/original/da583777c8d19f6b.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-03-15T20:09:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> If you need a way to create a light-weight scope to prevent unintentional bleed of \"global\" assignments, you can do tricks via <code>with</code> over a Proxy over globals.  </p><pre><code>globalThis.x = 'global.x';<br><br>let localGlobal = Object.create(globalThis);<br><br>let p = new Proxy(<br>    localGlobal,<br>    {<br>        has(obj, prop) {<br>            return true;<br>        },<br>        get(obj, prop) {<br>            if (prop === 'globalThis') { return localGlobal }<br>            return obj[prop];<br>        },<br>    }<br>);<br><br><br>with (p) {<br>    console.log('x before assignment', x);     // =&gt; global.x<br>    x = 'local-this';<br>    console.log('x after assignment', x);      // =&gt; local-this<br>    console.log('globalThis.x', globalThis.x); // =&gt; local-this<br>}<br>console.log('x outside `with`', x);            // =&gt; global.x<br><br></code></pre><p>Doesn't provide mutual suspicion and doesn't solve functions that return the global scope but keeps a lid on unintentional interference.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
